# RH/Zeta handoff for the TOE integration lane

This attachment is a **Lean-first analytic-domain handoff**.  Its authority for
machine-checked content is the `Lean/RiemannAnalytic.lean` aggregate and its 23
modules.  The reports are an available result snapshot and must not be read as
the current state of the separate RH specialist task.

## Scope for the TOE lane

Use this material to classify and, where justified, connect the analytic lane
to the common integration kernel.  Good candidates are generic finite-Gram,
Fourier-envelope, Poisson, coercivity, local-window, and ternary/channel
interfaces already shared with another domain.  Promote a connection only with
an explicit map plus a preservation/equivalence theorem.  Otherwise record a
typed dependency, socket, or boundary at its proper level.

## Explicit non-goals

Do **not** pursue a proof of RH or duplicate the specialist's analytic frontier:
complex continuation, finite-tail domination, short-interval prime estimates,
or uniform twisted-taper estimates.  Preserve their open status.  Do not infer
that a Lean theorem mirrors an Agda theorem merely because their names or prose
look related.

## Agda provenance

`Agda-reference/` is selected local source material only.  It is supplied to
guide faithful Lean mirrors and provenance checks; it is not a claim of Agda
typechecking in the Aristotle environment.  No Yang--Mills or Navier--Stokes
material is included.
